 ## Overview
-Voxel Space is a 2.5D rendering technique that generates a pseudo-3D environment by plotting vertical lines whose colors are sampled from a 2D color map and whose initial vertical positions are determined by a 2D depth map [S1, unofficial]. It avoids full 3D volumetric ray-casting or polygon rasterization, instead relying on pre-computed height and color data to simulate perspective [S1, unofficial].
+Voxel Space is a 2.5D rendering technique that generates a pseudo-3D environment by plotting vertical lines whose colors are sampled from a 2D color map and whose initial vertical positions are determined by a 2D depth map [S1, unofficial]. It avoids full 3D volumetric ray-casting or polygon rasterization, instead relying on pre-computed height and color data to simulate perspective [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel engines and games](47-voxel-engines-and-games.md) and differs from [Cascaded Voxel Volumes](4637-cascaded-voxel-volumes.md) by using fixed vertical lines rather than volumetric traversal [S1, unofficial].
 
